<%# Flash slot — replaced via turbo_stream when actions need to surface
    a transient message. :alert (errors) has always rendered here; :notice
    (success) now does too — the account pages need an explicit
    confirmation after redirecting away from the form that made the
    change, where the UI itself no longer shows it. This is app-wide, so
    Devise's own notices ("Signed in successfully.", "Signed out.", etc.)
    render with this styling too now — that's intentional, not a leak;
    if they ever prove noisy, blank those specific keys in
    config/locales/devise.en.yml rather than special-casing here. %>
<%# z-toast — the top of the ladder (see the stacking layers block in
    app/assets/tailwind/application.css). This started as z-[100], which painted
    the toast BEHIND the card modal and so hid it for exactly the branches that
    need it most: the comment form and the description editor both live inside the
    modal. The token also clears flatpickr's body-appended calendar (99999), so an
    error can't hide behind an open date picker either. Verified with
    elementFromPoint, not by eye. %>
<%#
  TIMEOUTS DIFFER BY SEVERITY, and that difference is the whole point of this
  partial's shape:

    errors  -> timeout 0 = never auto-dismiss (flash_controller only arms
               setTimeout when the value is positive)
    notices -> 5000ms, unchanged

  Every error-surfacing path in the app funnels through here (board forms, list
  rename, WIP limit, comments, update_description, Devise). A toast that removes
  itself after 5s made a real error indistinguishable from the silent failures
  those arcs were spent fixing — it outran a deliberate observer twice during
  browser verification. A success toast lingering is its own annoyance, so those
  keep the timer.

  Only ONE flash renders at a time into this replaceable #flash target, so a new
  flash replaces a lingering one. That's intended — no toast stack.

  Both keys are read for the error branch: :alert is what the app sets today,
  :error is accepted so a future caller can't have a message silently dropped.
%>
<% error_message = flash[:alert].presence || flash[:error].presence %>
<div id="flash" class="fixed top-20 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 z-toast w-full max-w-md px-4 pointer-events-none">
  <% if error_message %>
    <%# role="alert" so a persistent error is announced, not just shown —
        consistent with the a11y baseline this app maintains. %>
    <div class="bg-danger-600 text-white text-sm font-medium px-4 py-3 rounded-lg shadow-lg ring-1 ring-white/10 mb-2 pointer-events-auto flex items-start gap-2"
         role="alert"
         data-controller="flash"
         data-flash-timeout-value="0">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <span class="flex-1"><%= error_message %></span>
      <%= render "shared/flash_dismiss" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <% if flash[:notice].present? %>
    <div class="bg-success-100 text-success-600 text-sm font-medium px-4 py-3 rounded-lg shadow-lg mb-2 pointer-events-auto flex items-start gap-2"
         data-controller="flash"
         data-flash-timeout-value="5000">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <span class="flex-1"><%= flash[:notice] %></span>
      <%= render "shared/flash_dismiss" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
